{
  "goal": "Download Gauth and use it on one real problem or one set of your own notes today.",
  "angle": "Setting up to study feels productive, but nothing happens until you start the actual work. Gauth is the bridge between the two: snap the problem you are stuck on and follow the steps, or turn your notes into flashcards and a practice quiz. Every video shows the moment you stop prepping and start doing.",
  "hooks": [
    "when i'm having the best time planning my lock in and then remember i actually have to do the work now (on screen, then open Gauth by second 4)",
    "Desk is set up. Tabs are open. To-do list is color coded. I have done zero problems. Opening Gauth.",
    "I've been stuck on problem 4 for 40 minutes. Gauth just showed me the step I kept skipping.",
    "I turned 12 pages of my bio notes into a practice quiz on Gauth. Here's what I didn't actually know.",
    "Day 1 of studying for my calc final with Gauth instead of rewriting my notes for the third time."
  ],
  "mustInclude": [
    "Turn on the platform's paid partnership label, or put #ad in the caption.",
    "Put #gauthpartner in the caption.",
    "Say Gauth out loud or show the name on screen in the first 5 seconds.",
    "A real screen recording of Gauth on your own homework problem or your own notes. Show the step-by-step explanation, the flashcards or the practice quiz.",
    "Show yourself doing the work after the app: working the next problem, answering the flashcards or taking the quiz.",
    "A relatable study moment before the app appears, such as over-planning, a pretty desk or staring at one problem.",
    "End with one plain line telling viewers to download Gauth and try it on their own homework."
  ],
  "avoid": [
    "Any promise or hint of better grades, higher scores, passing or acing a test. Don't say it got you an A.",
    "Using Gauth during a test or exam, or any line suggesting it gets you through an exam. No cheating jokes.",
    "Framing it as the app doing your homework for you, or copying answers without showing the steps.",
    "Faked app screens or results. Record real use.",
    "Stats about Gauth's user numbers, app store rank or ownership. These are unverified.",
    "Naming or bashing other study apps.",
    "Hype words like game changer, insane or life-saving. Talk like a student, not an ad."
  ],
  "references": [
    {
      "title": "The Fake Productivity Hook Pulling Millions Of Views On Studytok (socialgrowthengineers.com)",
      "why": "This is the source for the main format and hook 1. The pre-study high, where you plan the lock-in and then realise you have to do the work, pulled 2M and 322.8K views. A related fake 27-hour study timelapse got 11.9M views and a newer version got 7.8M. The page says an app should feel like the bridge from about to be productive to actually doing it. A Tomo AI creator tried this format and it did not go viral, so make the turn to real work in the app clear and fast.",
      "url": ""
    },
    {
      "title": "Gauth - Learn AI",
      "why": "This is a community wiki and its claims are unverified. It says some schools and universities block Gauth and that AI-detection tools are improving. That is why every video shows learning the steps and never shows doing homework or exams for you.",
